time to, to make their tools look nice, but couldn't really identify any.

13
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.020
It seems that early humans shape their tools into teardrops simply because they

14
00:00:49.021 --> 00:00:52.780
like them better. That way throughout our history,

15
00:00:52.781 --> 00:00:54.860
the definition of beauty has changed a lot.

16
00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.140
Ideals have shifted or turned into their opposite,

17
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.300
but beyond individual and contemporary,

18
00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:05.610
some things have never really gone outta fashion. The golden ratio,

19
00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:10.010
symmetry or fractal patterns can be found in the art and architecture of

20
00:01:10.011 --> 00:01:12.050
cultures from our beginnings to today.

21
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:17.210
Humans seem to be in mysterious inherent agreement about the beauty of certain

22
00:01:17.211 --> 00:01:21.370
