A deformed Wheater may not be safe to eat.

33
00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.700
<v 2>Asymmetrical face is more likely to belong to a healthy and fertile mating</v>

34
00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:16.620
partner because symmetry is so common in fauna and flora.

35
00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.700
It's extremely familiar to our brain.

36
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.970
It helped our ancestors evaluate their environment more easily and quickly

37
00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:29.010
to danger things that help us survive. Activate the reward center in our brain,

38
00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:33.490
recognizing signals of safety and nutrition trigger, nice feelings in us.

39
00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:37.610
<v 0>So our sense of beauty probably evolved from pattern recognition,</v>

40
00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.490
but it goes way beyond that.

41
00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:44.010
Now humans seem to have evolved an instinct for beauty that is deeply high

